title the ring that destroys by name
prompt Keaton said kg finish glow then mand -- this is the second half.
think mand is custody code: a capability table and three rings that decide retention, audit a read, and destroy a key. A reason is worth most exactly here, so I wrote these more carefully than the lowering passes.
obs The sharpest one wrote itself. mand_ring3 copies a subject into a fixed buffer before inserting a key, and this ring destroys keys BY SUBJECT -- so a truncated name does not merely mislabel, it destroys the wrong key. That is what the bound is for, and nothing above the assert had ever said so.
obs Two more of the same weight. A grant onto an inactive capability slot hands a capability to a dependent that is not there to receive it while the count still rises. And a hold in ring 2 can only be placed on something already eligible, so reaching that line from another standing means a hold is being read as an override rather than a pause.
obs tally_copy's disjointness assert is the reason the function exists at all rather than a bare memcpy, and the invariant line now says that instead of restating the comparison.
obs run_self_test in capabilities.rye carries an underscore the role words do not match, and reachability caught it anyway -- 15 of the file's 31 asserts binned as proof without a name to go on. The bin earning its keep on a case it was not told about.
obs mand reads 61 of 61. Tree 93%, gap 1,124.
loom sweep room=mand files=5 blocks=40 asserts=61 pct=0->100 tree_gap=1187->1124
file mand/capabilities.rye 15 blocks over the capability table
file mand/mand_ring3.rye 10 blocks over key insert, seal, open and destroy
file mand/mand_ring2.rye 9 blocks over retention standing and its audit
file mand/mand_ring1.rye 4 blocks over the audit trail and the see seam
file mand/tally_copy.rye 2 blocks -- the disjointness that is the function's whole reason
file construction/ITINERARY.md mand closed, crypto and linengrow named
recommend keep-going crypto holds 271 at 57.5% and may be another placement story like glow -- worth reading a few before sweeping
